0..68 Comment "// Streams as codata: a family known by its observations, built by a"
69..141 Comment "// copattern block that answers each one, and taken apart by observing a"
142..216 Comment "// thunk of it. A recursive call claiming `>` is productive when it is the"
217..286 Comment "// whole arm of a copattern block: each observation yields before the"
287..359 Comment "// function runs again, so the fixpoint needs no termination claim. What"
360..419 Comment "// refuses is in `../../pathological/codata/streams.gandr`."
420..422 Comment "//"
423..437 Comment "// - see: #644"
438..464 Comment "// - see: #1499 — `ones`"
